case ptab-ipr-defense
uses ptab-patent-trial-appeal-board ^0.1.0, cafc ^0.1.0
as_of 2026-08-26
summary "IPR defense by a patent owner at the PTAB (35 U.S.C. §§311-319), from the Patent Owner Preliminary Response through a final written decision, with appeal to the CAFC."
notes "Protagonist is the PATENT OWNER defending against a petitioner's inter partes review, not the petitioner. Uses `ptab-patent-trial-appeal-board` + `cafc` (links.json's `cafc@ptab` instance supplies the appeal, remanding only back to the Board). The events replay to the notice of filing date accorded (the POPR clock start), leaving the matter at the § 315(b) time-bar fact, which `facts` resolves into `popr-window`, so the graph begins where the patent owner's own defense choices begin, skipping the pre-suit/petition-filing steps that are the petitioner's decisions, not the defense's. JUDGMENT CALL (perspective mapping): this pack's actor vocabulary (schemaVersion 2 as of a later migration, but `roles` is still just the default identity mapping — applicant→self, examiner/office→nature, either→nature; the pack has no dedicated patent-owner actor) uses `applicant` for the PETITIONER's moves (files the petition, moves for joinder, replies, opposes amendment — verified against every `actor: applicant` edge in the pack) and buckets the patent owner's own moves (file/waive POPR, file/skip response, settle, move to amend, waive oral argument, request rehearing/Director review, decide whether to appeal) together with genuinely joint/neutral steps under one `either` actor — the pack has no actor distinguishing 'patent owner's own choice' from 'joint/neutral event'. `perspective` below remaps `applicant -> opponent` (the petitioner becomes the adversary we solve against) and `either -> self` (so the patent owner's actual defense choices are exposed to `explain`/`solve`), leaving `examiner`/`office` at their default `nature` (the Board and the Federal Circuit acting adjudicatively). This is the closest reading the CURRENT pack data supports without editing pack content (out of this scenario's scope); it necessarily also treats some genuinely joint/neutral `either` edges as 'our' choice — flagged here rather than silently assumed. A cleaner fix (a dedicated `patent-owner` actor in the pack) is a pack-content change for whoever owns `packs/ptab-patent-trial-appeal-board.json` next, not this scenario. SECOND JUDGMENT CALL (payoffs): several CAFC-side and post-FWD PTAB terminals (`appeal-forfeited-unappealed`, `cafc@ptab::window-blown-ptab`/`dismissed-failure-to-prosecute`/`rule36-affirmance`/`affirmed`/`dismissed-jurisdictional-defect`/`cert-not-sought`/`cert-denied`/`cert-granted`) are reachable regardless of which prior FWD outcome preceded them — a known engine/pack-content limitation (docs/CRITIQUE.md, 'Markov on the node': the graph has no memory of which FWD led here). Rather than inventing false precision, this scenario assigns those a flat mid-range illustrative value ($1,500,000, half of the $3,000,000 illustrative patent value used for a clean win) and says so per-terminal below instead of leaving it unstated. All dollar figures assume an illustrative $3,000,000 patent value (this patent's licensing/enforcement value if it survives intact) and a $700/hr blended rate; neither is sourced (no real matter identified) — override both per actual matter."

source "35 U.S.C. §319 — appeal of a PTAB final written decision to the Federal Circuit" {
  url "https://www.law.cornell.edu/uscode/text/35/319"
}

source "35 U.S.C. §315(e) — IPR estoppel attaching at final written decision" {
  url "https://www.law.cornell.edu/uscode/text/35/315"
}

perspective owner

parties {
  owner: either Corporation
  petitioner: applicant Corporation
}

events {
  2021-03-02 PatentGranted() on owner
  2025-09-15 ComplaintServed() on petitioner
  2026-06-01 IprPetitionFiled() by petitioner
  2026-06-18 FilingDateNoticed() on owner
}

// Complaint served 2025-09-15, petition filed 2026-06-01: inside the
// 35 U.S.C. § 315(b) one-year bar.
facts { petition-time-bar-check: e-time-bar-clear }

stakes {
  ptab-patent-trial-appeal-board::ipr-time-barred: 3_000_000.usd
  ptab-patent-trial-appeal-board::claims-disclaimed-preinstitution: 1_500_000.usd
  ptab-patent-trial-appeal-board::institution-denied-merits: 3_000_000.usd
  ptab-patent-trial-appeal-board::institution-denied-fintiv: 3_000_000.usd
  ptab-patent-trial-appeal-board::ipr-terminated-settlement: 2_000_000.usd
  ptab-patent-trial-appeal-board::adverse-judgment-terminal: 0.usd
  ptab-patent-trial-appeal-board::fwd-all-unpatentable: 0.usd
  ptab-patent-trial-appeal-board::fwd-all-confirmed: 3_000_000.usd
  ptab-patent-trial-appeal-board::fwd-mixed: 1_500_000.usd
  ptab-patent-trial-appeal-board::appeal-forfeited-unappealed: 1_500_000.usd
  cafc@ptab::window-blown-ptab: 1_500_000.usd
  cafc@ptab::settled-in-mediation: 2_000_000.usd
  cafc@ptab::dismissed-failure-to-prosecute: 1_500_000.usd
  cafc@ptab::rule36-affirmance: 1_500_000.usd
  cafc@ptab::affirmed: 1_500_000.usd
  cafc@ptab::reversed: 3_000_000.usd
  cafc@ptab::affirmed-in-part-reversed-in-part: 1_500_000.usd
  cafc@ptab::dismissed-jurisdictional-defect: 1_500_000.usd
  cafc@ptab::remanded-to-ptab: 1_500_000.usd
  cafc@ptab::cert-not-sought: 1_500_000.usd
  cafc@ptab::cert-denied: 1_500_000.usd
  cafc@ptab::cert-granted: 1_500_000.usd
}

analysis { params: { rate: 700, opp_rate: 650 } }
